Description: Stereo icon themes: an icon the theme has in stereo gives each eye its view
 .
 The edition's Qt draws a window once per eye while it shows depth inside it, and names
 the eye on the window (_q_stereo_eye: Qt Widgets while it paints that eye, Qt Quick
 while it polishes and synchronizes it). KIconEngine now loads each eye's view of an
 icon's stereo picture in those passes: from the widget window being painted, or from an item that names the
 eye it asks for on the application (_q_stereo_icon_eye). The view gets the plain icon's state effect and overlays and is
 cached per eye. Outside those passes, and for an icon without a stereo picture, every
 load is the plain icon as before, so a 2D output is unchanged. The stereo picture comes
 from the first theme in the order of inheritance that has the icon, as with
 loadStereoIcon(). No depth is added: each view is the picture the theme carries.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
